# A second anvil pin, scoped to one binary: the L1 of the Glamsterdam gas check (L1_GAS_RULES=amsterdam,
# the upgrade-test-glamsterdam job in anvil-interop-ci.yaml).
#
# Consumed by:
#   - l1-contracts/test/anvil-interop/scripts/install-amsterdam-anvil.sh
#     (in CI through .github/actions/install-amsterdam-anvil)
#
# Everything else, forge, cast, every other anvil, builds, hashes, chain states and Docker included, stays on
# FOUNDRY_VERSION in foundry-versions.env. This pin lives in its own file so that bumping it does not touch
# the coverage recipe or the Docker base image, which both hash foundry-versions.env.
#
# A nightly because the newest stable release (v1.8.5) accepts `--hardfork amsterdam` without applying
# EIP-8037/2780/7976/8038. Bump to the first stable release that implements them; the canary in
# l1-contracts/test/anvil-interop/src/daemons/amsterdam-l1.ts fails on a build that does not.
#
# Keep this file shell-sourceable: `KEY=value`, no spaces, no expansion.
AMSTERDAM_ANVIL_TAG=nightly-9861e3f7f08aec8f7b8fa77ff5ae5d5f6cdf79b3
AMSTERDAM_ANVIL_ASSET_LINUX_AMD64=foundry_nightly_linux_amd64.tar.gz
AMSTERDAM_ANVIL_SHA256_LINUX_AMD64=cd1e669c40f96013388cfb603a3ec7040e827b1787f797365fdda89e755c4697
AMSTERDAM_ANVIL_ASSET_DARWIN_ARM64=foundry_nightly_darwin_arm64.tar.gz
AMSTERDAM_ANVIL_SHA256_DARWIN_ARM64=3888687d7e3b79472ed76694471af2752e0c2ef258de1cb3aa35efcd0a961954
